The difference is that in previous versions (as I understand it) nurses did
the equivalent of an extra healing potion, so they could up your maximum
hit points by two points.  Now your max can only go up by one point (scaled
down to normal healing?), but other than that, yeah - it still works.

Thus, one scam I had going for a while was to go through characters until
I got a wizard that started with a scroll of genocide and a potion of water.
I'd then run around dipping the potion of water into fountains (or dropping
it on a chaotic altar if I was lucky) until it became unholy water.  #dip
the scroll in the potion, find a nice room with doors that I could close,
take off all the armor and wield nothing, and read that scroll!  Hey presto:
with a little bit of patience, I had a 2nd level character with fifty hit
points!

